{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>All that He had made, and behold, it was very good.</b> The end of existence as a whole is very good — more so than the particular ends that are directed toward it." "<b>The sixth day.</b> The first that was the beginning for every sixth day, on which all labors are completed in order to rest on the Sabbath, as it says (Exodus 20:9–10): וְעָשִׂיתָ כָּל מְלַאכְתֶּךָ וְיוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי שַׁבָּת — and on the seventh day, Sabbath."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:12:41.847095072Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}